Pass a string to run only tests whose **full path contains it**. With these tests:

```rust
#[test] fn add_two_and_two() { ... }
#[test] fn add_three_and_two() { ... }
#[test] fn one_hundred() { ... }
```

A few tests may be expensive: a long simulation, a network call. Mark them with **`#[ignore]`** so normal runs skip them, and run them when you want:

```rust
#[test]
#[ignore = "takes about a minute"]
fn expensive_test() {
    // ...
}
```
